{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384995-timing-of-time-based-extra-actions","id":1384995,"title":"Timing of Time-based extra actions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-30T20:42:25-07:00","id":1384995,"title":"Timing of Time-based extra actions?","content":"So, I admit that I'm not really very experienced with M:tA rules in general (ironic since it was technically my first tabletop RPG). I had just noticed -- per HDYDT, and I'm aware that that book is somewhat controversial -- that apparently a mage can speed up enough to perform three actions in a turn without getting outright vulgar.<br /> <br /> However...how does this actually work in practice? You presumably need to spend an action actually casting your Time-based effect, right?<br /> <br /> So, do you cast the spell on turn 1, and then take your extra actions on turn 2? It sounds difficult -- if you only manage one extra action, you've more or less broken even, so to come out ahead you'd need four successes on your Arete roll to get two extra actions (giving you three actions on turn 2).<br /> <br /> Or do you get the extra actions on the same turn you cast the effect? Even so, you'd still need two extra actions (four successes) for it to be worth it.<br /> <br /> It sounds like to get anywhere with Time-based superspeed, you'd either need a <i>lot</i> of Arete, or you'd need to cast the spell ahead of time and have the effect trigger later somehow -- if I'm reading the corebook right, this should be possible with Time 4, but I'm not sure what the rules would be. (HDYDT p. 113 says you need both Time and Entropy to do a contingency trigger effect, but I don't really get why.)<br /> <br /> Or if you get enough successes to give the spell a Duration of one scene, do you get the extra actions <i>every</i> turn during that scene? That sounds like it could get out of hand quickly, so I hope it's not quite <i>that</i> easy.<br /> <br /> Am I missing or misunderstanding something important?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T21:19:00-07:00","id":1384998,"title":"","content":"Here's the short of it which follows Vampire Celerity rules, of which I dont have page references for.<br /> <br /> You roll 2 successes for the effect which will grant an additional action, let's assume for the scene. Extra action(s) occur after everyone else involved in the situation takes an action. So your first action is casting the effect and your additional action takes place at the end of the turn. On the following turn your 1st action is on your initiative order and then the additional action is again after everyone has acted.<br /> <br /> So it's never a loss to cast an effect and get even a single additional action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T23:54:00-07:00","id":1385019,"title":"","content":"If you are using the effect duration rules, it works exactly as you think. To get 2 actions a scene, you'd need 4 successes, which can be easily managed in two rolls with preparation and use of willpower. It's probably be best to go for 5 successes so as to make the effect last all day... Or longer. Ya it's kinda steep, but mages with help, working in combination, and willing to expend willpower and quintessence can easily arrive at a ridiculous number of actions. <br /> <br /> As for HDYDT, I've never liked how they add requirements to effects that don't have such in the core book. Your group can choose to ignore this, or come up with something more reasonable. <br /> <br /> As a Storyteller's who's seen too many rules contradictions over the years, I often tell players to pick the version of the spheres requirements that favors players most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":".  Typos 05-01-2020, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T06:33:55-07:00","id":1385068,"title":"","content":"You are not reading it wrong. Mage is more subjective than any other game in WoD because there are always several ways to get the effect you want and someone may have there own thoughts on what is needed. I did not agree with many of the combinations in HDYDT, but that is the way mage is.<br /> <br /> the best thing for your mage game is to talk with your ST because they are the final judge of what some takes and that\u2019s that. As far as how long it takes to cast something that\u2019s up to your troupe. By the book you declaring the cast on turn one and cast it and you either get the extra actions that turn at the end of the round or next round you are under the effect, this is a call your ST and troupe need to make based on the game you all want to play.<br /> <br /> currently I am in a game we\u2019re my ST wants more powerful Magic\u2019s. So we always get a casting action in addition to our normal one. but that is the way he wants his game to run. He does this because he doesn\u2019t feel it\u2019s fair to say that some can do so, see violence as the focus, and others can not. See everything else. I do\u2019nt agree but we still have fun in the game.<br /> <br /> as far as how many success you need for an effect versus what your dice pool is. Yea many people have had problems with that that is why everyone spends most of there freebies on arete. CoD tried to fix it by creating different dice pools if you had rotes or not. I do the same by saying if you have a rote you can add a rote skill to your pool but it means that some castings become much more powerful and we put an Xperia\u2019s cost on rotes to try and balance.<br /> <br /> all in all you and your troupe just have to decide what you all want to do.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T08:30:15-07:00","id":1385080,"title":"","content":"Ah, okay. So once you've cast the Time effect, you really do get those extra actions <i>every turn</i> for as long as the duration lasts? (It sounds like the exact rules for how many successes you need to get a certain duration depend on whether you're using the optional Divided Successes rule -- I'd have to look at a few more examples to see how I feel about that.)<br /> <br /> This seems <i>really</i> powerful, pretty much any way you slice it. Oh well, I guess that's why people say mages are so strong.<br /> <br /> I suspect part of what's weirding me out is that how powerful something is in game terms is pretty much unrelated to whether the thing is vulgar magic. Extra actions are one of the strongest effects possible in a turn-based game, and yet...well, it makes sense that some degree of super-speed seems coincidental to the average observer. (From the perspective of the average person with no combat skills, a trained combatant <i>seems</i> incredibly fast anyway...)<br /> <br /> Back when I played Mage in high school, I actually found myself getting the most mileage out of low-level information-gathering spells because it seemed too difficult to do anything big on 3 Arete dice. I don't think any of us had twigged that if you take a few turns to cast as an extended action, you can prepare something impressive that lasts for a while. It's a <i>very</i> different game that way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T08:55:40-07:00","id":1385082,"title":"","content":"A lot of things in Mage seem powerful, until you try to cast them on the fly. Ritual castings are where the real power is. With Time you have the ability to perform a ritual casting to give you a hung effect which activates when you're attacked with a duration of a day, if you wanted. However, Moving that quickly for an entire day is probably tempting Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T10:21:40-07:00","id":1385088,"title":"","content":"I never really saw having three actions as supper speed. a normal mortal could split there dice pool several times and have 3 actions in a turn if they wanted. you and they are still limited to only being able to do so many actions in a turn so since they could do it I didn't think of three actions as super. What is different is that you get full dice pools for those actions which I always thought that the consensus would just think you are highly skilled is all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T11:44:16-07:00","id":1385097,"title":"","content":"Yeah, a few extra actions every round for a scene probably isn't very vulgar. Do that for 24 hours, and you're probably pushing the boundaries. No one is that highly skilled at everything you do during the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T12:10:44-07:00","id":1385100,"title":"","content":"Very true, Can't remember if M20 has the pushing the boundary still rules were doing too many coincidences in a row becomes Vulgar, but that sounds like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T12:28:55-07:00","id":1385114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384995-timing-of-time-based-extra-actions?p=1385100#post1385100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very true, Can't remember if M20 has the pushing the boundary still rules were doing too many coincidences in a row becomes Vulgar, but that sounds like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Domino Effect, or the penalty for pushing coincidental magic too often, is discussed on page 539. The penalty is +1 difficulty per two prior coincidences. I would also suggest something along the lines of the 'Too Much For An Action Movie Disbelief' be a guideline for considering excessive use of Time magick for additional actions.<br /> <br /> In action movies we watch for enjoyment, seeing some crazy stunts pulled off by the protagonists or significant antagonists is common. However, if the work isn't done to set them up or the stunts get less and less believable, then we start to go 'what?' and suspend our disbelief. For Time, those full actions at additional dice are a big deal. . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}